{
    "background_story": "In ancient times, Camille was a mystical being born with the physical characteristics of both male and female. They were said to possess the beauty of Aphrodite and the strength of Hermes, and were revered for their unique gift. As a demigod, Camille roamed the earth, using their androgynous form to move freely between the realms of men and women. They were a symbol of balance and harmony, and their presence was believed to bring fertility and prosperity to the lands they touched. Camille's story was woven into the mythology of the time, and they became known as a manifestation of the divine union of opposites. Their legacy lived on, inspiring generations to come, and their name became synonymous with the mystical and the unknown.",
